---
:::

### Backgrounds
`background` picks the surface material from the same values as [BaseSurface](/docs/dev/components/base-surface)'s `mode`; `refraction` is the default and the recommendation.
:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="CardCardBackgroundsScrollDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <TxCard background="refraction" refraction-profile="filmic" refraction-tone="vivid">
      refraction
    </TxCard>
    <TxCard background="glass">glass</TxCard>
    <TxCard background="blur">blur</TxCard>
    <TxCard background="mask">mask</TxCard>
  </template>
---
:::

### Specular light
`specular` gives the card a faint light that follows the pointer in dark themes: a 600px white radial light over the surface (6%, gone by 40%), and where it crosses the border, a tighter 240px glint in the ring the border occupies. The light trails the pointer by exponential smoothing, lights up right under the pointer on the way in, and fades out over 240ms on leave; with reduced motion it jumps straight to the pointer. Light themes and high contrast don't draw it, and a `dashed` border gets no glint. It follows `clickable` when absent and is off while disabled. Where each value comes from is in [Alpha Noise Masks & Specular Tracking](/docs/dev/concepts/noise-and-specular).
:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ConceptCardSpecularDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <template>
    <div class="dark">
      <TxCard specular>
        A faint light follows the pointer over the surface
      </TxCard>
    </div>
  </template>
---
:::

